    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nTriggering any deprecation warning (e.g. calling vim.hl.on_yank) causes the msg_show UI event handler to throw:\n\nError in \"msg_show\" UI event handler (ns=nvim.ui2):\nLua: …/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua:243: Invalid 'end_col': out of range\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_buf_set_extmark'\n\t…/ui2/messages.lua:243: in function 'expand_msg'\n\t…/ui2/messages.lua:335: in function 'set_target_pos'\n\t…/ui2/messages.lua:396: in function 'show_msg'\n\t…/ui2/messages.lua:496: in function 'handler'\n\tvim/_core/ui2:169: in function 'ui_callback'\n\tvim/_core/ui2:218: in function <vim/_core/ui2:210>\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_echo'\n\t…/editor:1394: in function 'truncated_echo'\n\t…/editor:1401: in function '_truncated_echo_once'\n\t…/editor:1463: in function 'deprecate'\n\t…/runtime/lua/vim/hl.lua:223: in function 'on_yank'\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\nCall a deprecated function that routes through vim.deprecate() — :lua vim.hl.on_yank() reproduces it for me.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe deprecation warning renders without the message handler erroring.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-nightly+ b997265\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno idea\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS Tahoe\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nnix nightly overlay",
